{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Point"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(json:warnings:)","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(start:end:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/jsonObject"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONObjectEncodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueDecodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueEncodable-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/domrange"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONObjectEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueDecodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/SQ","doc:\/\/Readium\/SH"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary point."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"window.selection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that designates a child text node."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary points."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"